    "topic_path": "Root/ACT 1/Scene 2/Horatio Father Methinks",
    "content": "I prithee, do not mock me, fellow student. I think it was to see my mother’s wedding. Indeed, my lord, it followed hard upon. Thrift, thrift, Horatio. The funeral baked meats\n Did coldly furnish forth the marriage tables. Would I had met my dearest foe in heaven\n Or ever I had seen that day, Horatio! My father—methinks I see my father. Where, my lord? In my mind’s eye, Horatio. I saw him once. He was a goodly king. He was a man. Take him for all in all,\n I shall not look upon his like again. My lord, I think I saw him yesternight. Saw who? My lord, the King your father. The King my father? Season your admiration for a while\n With an attent ear, till I may deliver\n Upon the witness of these gentlemen\n This marvel to you. For God’s love, let me hear!",
